From: David Mosberger <davidm@napali.hpl.hp.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jul 2002 01:16:05 +0000
Subject: [Linux-ia64] [patch] important performance bug fix
Message-Id: <marc-linux-ia64-105590701905777@msgid-missing>
List-Id: <linux-ia64.vger.kernel.org>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="iso-8859-1"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
To: linux-ia64@vger.kernel.org

The patch below fixes an encoding table bug for the indirect call
instruction of ia64 (br.call b1=B2).  The old encoding was wrong in
one bit.  Fortunately, the bug affects only performance on Itanium 2,
it does not affect correctness for any existing ia64 implementation.
Even so, it's important that this bug gets fixed asap since the
incorrect encoding causes bad branch-prediction performance, which can
slow down execution significantly (up to 20% in microbenchmarks).

The patch below consists of two pieces: changes to ia64-opc-b.c and
the corresponding changes to ia64-asmtab.c.  If you wish, you can
ignore the second part and simply rebuild ia64-asmtab yourself (you
need to configure binutils with --enable-maintainer-mode for this to
work).

	--david

PS: It is possible that the test-suite needs to be updated accordingly.
    I don't know how to do this.

2002-07-12  David Mosberger  <davidm@hpl.hp.com>

	* ia64-opc-b.c (bWhc): New macro.
	(mWhc): Ditto.
	(OpPaWhcD): Ditto.
	(ia64_opcodes_b): Correct patterns for indirect call instructions to use
	3-bit "wh" field.

